  "answer_text": "To quantify the contribution of external room light entering the spectrometer, one must isolate the signal that reaches the detector when the system is open to ambient light but without the laser firing, and subtract the intrinsic electronic noise (dark current) of the CCD.\n\n1. **Acquire a \"normal\" background spectrum**: Call `acquire_spectrum` with the shutter open (`shutter='auto'`) and the laser off. This capture includes both the room light leaking into the system and the detector's dark current.\n2. **Acquire a \"dark\" spectrum**: Call `acquire_spectrum` with `shutter='close'`. This blocks all photons from reaching the CCD, capturing only the electronic dark current.\n\nThe contribution of the external light is then determined by subtracting the dark frame from the normal background frame.\n\n```json\n{\"plan\": [\"acquire_spectrum\", \"acquire_spectrum\"], \"decision\": \"normal_minus_dark\"}\n```",
